  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the limit as\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-9\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{1-4x}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{4x-1}.\n$$\n\nThe numerator here is a bounded, oscillating function with\n\n$$\n|9\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x|\\le 9.\n$$\n\nHowever, the denominator $4x-1$ grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty .$ So the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-9\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{1-4x}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{4x-1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac{-9\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{1-4x},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951126/assets/64700491874195711ad7291ce0471561df307bd099b5b8a38c33269cf08f21ab.png)",
